<section image-layout="blank" id="O_FkwMFPav" background-color="heading"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="kLFIWCsbx4" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><p role="eyebrow">Project Meridian · handover pack</p><h1 font-size="44pt">Project Meridian: handover pack for the incoming owner</h1><p font-size="lg">The project position, operating model, settled decisions, open calls and actions you inherit on 1 October.</p><spacer size="24pt"></spacer><p font-size="sm">Kestrel Data · Priya Raghunathan · 23 September 2026</p></grid-item><grid-item id="u6Z2xRWTbl" padding="0" colspan="24"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/SJYnkmAfMHlcInU344tf2.png" saved-media-id="4s9oo3up66oehuz" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="operational-still-life" alt="Editorial studio photograph of modular warm-white paper blocks connected by operational-blue cord, with a graphite handover tab passing from one precise arrangement to the next, signal-amber clip marking an unresolved gate and field-sage block marking completed work, soft directional daylight, generous negative space, no text, lettering, people, logos or screens." meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="yBcJyV7uJ8"><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="MIQjKnf3xf" vertical-align="center" colspan="38"><p role="eyebrow">MERIDIAN · READER NOTE · N-01</p><h1>This is a fictional worked example</h1><p>Kestrel Data, Project Meridian, and every name, figure, contract and date in this pack are invented to demonstrate what a complete handover looks like. Nothing here describes a real company or real results.</p><p>Figures marked <i>assumption</i> are illustrative planning inputs, not measurements. Everything else is presented as the project's own recorded numbers.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ZSBx5cg-uT" background-color="surface" vertical-align="center" colspan="22"><labels><label variant="solid">FICTIONAL</label></labels><h3>Kestrel Data</h3><p font-size="sm">B2B workforce analytics · 310 staff · 1,180 customers</p><h4>Project</h4><p font-size="sm">Replace the homegrown billing system with Nomad Billing.</p><h4>Pack written</h4><p font-size="sm">23 September 2026 · Priya Raghunathan, outgoing owner</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="EeapnbTDhO"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="lpUSAYvIYx"><p role="eyebrow">MERIDIAN · EXECUTIVE READ · S-01</p><h2>Where Meridian stands today, in one page</h2><aside variant="warning"><p><b>Overall: amber.</b> Delivery is on track; budget and one dependency are not.</p></aside><table col-widths="[18,22,60]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td><p>Area</p></td><td><p>Status</p></td><td><p>Position at 23 September 2026</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Phase 1</b></p></td><td><p>Live</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Catalog, invoicing and payments have been live since 4 May. All new business has used Nomad since that date.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Phase 2</b></p></td><td><p>62% complete</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">707 of 1,140 eligible accounts moved. Eight waves remain, ending 14 January 2027.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Phase 3</b></p></td><td><p>Not started</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Revenue recognition and dunning target 26 February 2027.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Budget</b></p></td><td><p>Approval pending</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">$2.40M approved, $1.52M spent and $2.61M forecast: 8.75% over.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Largest risk</b></p></td><td><p>Red</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">The 88 complex accounts have no proven migration pattern.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="1MH9smfs0I"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="rqYMor72Kc"><p role="eyebrow">MERIDIAN · PACK MAP · N-02</p><h2>How this pack runs</h2><grid divider="sm neutral-border" marker="number" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-inline-size: 32pt; --marker-gap: 14pt;"><grid-item id="uG04tWd8Pk" padding="10pt 0"><h4>Context and scope</h4><p>Why Meridian exists, what it covers and what it deliberately does not.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="EhoFuGLjgh" padding="10pt 0"><h4>Where things stand</h4><p>Status by workstream, migration numbers, budget and invoice quality.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="7z_2U7uQpo" padding="10pt 0"><h4>How it runs</h4><p>Cadence, systems, access, the incident runbook and the vendor.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="14gw75MROQ" padding="10pt 0"><h4>People and decisions</h4><p>Owners, settled decisions, open calls, risks and dependencies.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="VE34UQSJFV" padding="10pt 0"><h4>Your first ninety days</h4><p>Sequenced actions, unanswered questions and the handover terms.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="4tSta4I2zt" background-color="heading"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="jxMlexOCms" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><p role="eyebrow">SECTION 01 · CONTEXT AND SCOPE</p><h1>Context and scope</h1><p font-size="lg">Why billing became the constraint, what Meridian changes and where its boundary stays fixed.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ZBlPV-L2Qp" padding="0" colspan="24"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/Crhldlxf7xoZCqV5_CvOd.png" saved-media-id="rtnx2via3gzzbll" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="operational-still-life" alt="Editorial studio photograph of a constrained modular paper system, one narrow graphite channel limiting several operational-blue paper paths while warm-white blocks wait behind it, a signal-amber tab marking the bottleneck, soft directional daylight, precise clean arrangement, no text, lettering, people, logos or screens." meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="pSI397qvbd"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="pwHBLZRita"><p role="eyebrow">CONTEXT · CASE FOR CHANGE · C-01</p><h2>Billing was the constraint on every pricing decision Kestrel wanted to make</h2><p>BillingSvc was written in 2017 for one annual seat-based plan sold in USD. It never became a platform.</p><grid spacing="small" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="UJ9iNf9gDr" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><h4>Pricing stayed frozen</h4><p font-size="sm">Usage-based and hybrid plans needed engineering work per contract. Sales maintained 41 bespoke arrangements by hand.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="yQSczZVaia" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><h4>Close consumed the month</h4><p font-size="sm">Finance spent 9 of 10 close days reconciling invoices in spreadsheets.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="J0JnCX1lao" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><h4>Customers saw the errors</h4><p font-size="sm">In June 2026, 4.8% of invoices needed a manual correction.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="XzOdoIZNdM" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><h4>Ownership never formed</h4><p font-size="sm">Two part-time engineers, no roadmap and no test coverage on proration.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">The board approved Meridian in December 2025 on a three-year payback. That payback was an assumption built from the 2025 cost base, not a measured result.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="0ANv-ege4b"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="SfnB4Vpb6y"><p role="eyebrow">CONTEXT · IN SCOPE · C-02</p><h2>What Meridian covers</h2><table col-widths="[25,75]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td><p>Capability</p></td><td><p>Committed scope</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Subscription catalog</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Plans, add-ons, ramps and discounts configurable without a deploy.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Invoicing and payments</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Generation, delivery, card and ACH collection, and credit notes.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Tax</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Calculation and filing data through Tessera Tax across 34 jurisdictions.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Dunning</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Automated retry and escalation for failed payments in Phase 3.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Revenue recognition</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">ASC 606 schedules generated from contract terms in Phase 3.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Self-serve checkout</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">The public purchase flow, re-pointed to Nomad.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Account migration</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Move 1,140 eligible accounts and 4,190 subscriptions off BillingSvc. The 40 perpetual-licence accounts are carved out of the 1,180-customer total, so every migration figure uses 1,140.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="aMU24X-EiW"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="u_31OIvtK5"><p role="eyebrow">CONTEXT · EXCLUSIONS · C-03</p><h2>What Meridian deliberately does not cover</h2><p>Each exclusion was a steering-committee decision, not an oversight. Resist requests to absorb them.</p><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="VuV3oam7iE" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><h3>Systems owned elsewhere</h3><ul><li><b>Usage metering:</b> Data Platform owns the pipeline; Meridian only consumes its API.</li><li><b>Sales-assisted quoting:</b> stays in Salesforce CPQ under Deal Desk.</li><li><b>Commission calculation:</b> remains in the Sales Ops spreadsheet model.</li></ul></grid-item><grid-item id="oO30rmyI_0" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><h3>Deferred or carved out</h3><ul><li><b>Multi-entity consolidation:</b> deferred to FY28 with the EMEA entity work.</li><li><b>Alternative payments:</b> no wallets, crypto or regional rails beyond SEPA.</li><li><b>40 perpetual-licence accounts:</b> run off in BillingSvc through FY28 and never migrate. Their exclusion gives the 1,140 eligible base.</li></ul></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="r4iSZtcmhL"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="bXF0wzFCCY"><p role="eyebrow">CONTEXT · DELIVERY SHAPE · C-04</p><h2>Five phases, one cutover per wave, sixteen waves in total</h2><smart-layout variant="minimalTimeline" orientation="horizontal" cell-size="15"><smart-layout-item><h4>Phase 0 · Jan–Mar 2026</h4><p>Vendor selection, contract and data-model mapping. Complete.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Phase 1 · Apr–May</h4><p>Catalog, invoicing and payments live for new business on 4 May. Complete.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Phase 2 · Jun–Jan</h4><p>Fortnightly Thursday waves: 1–8 ran 4 Jun–10 Sep; 9–16 run 8 Oct–14 Jan. In flight.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Phase 3 · Nov–Feb</h4><p>Revenue recognition and dunning overlap the last waves. Target 26 February. Not started.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Phase 4 · FY28</h4><p>BillingSvc decommission. Not funded; date undecided.</p></smart-layout-item></smart-layout><aside><p>No wave ran on 24 September; the slot was held so the complex-account design could land first.</p></aside></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="A0-SwVRjRj" vertical-align="center" background-color="accent"><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="MjeuprqrkQ" vertical-align="center" colspan="18"><display size="lg">02</display></grid-item><grid-item id="sA3B3Ldfbw" vertical-align="center" colspan="42"><p role="eyebrow">WHERE THINGS STAND</p><h1>Where things stand</h1><p font-size="lg">Workstream health, the migration remainder, forecast cost and invoice quality.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="8v9aN7rfLG"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="ChMkUOQwIt"><p role="eyebrow">STATUS · WORKSTREAM REGISTER · S-02</p><h2>Status by workstream</h2><table col-widths="[25,13,45,17]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td><p>Workstream</p></td><td><p>Status</p></td><td><p>Current position</p></td><td><p>Owner</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Migration waves</b></p></td><td><p>Green</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">707 of 1,140 accounts live. Wave 9 ships 8 October.</p></td><td><p>Hannah Blum</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Complex accounts</b></p></td><td><p>Red</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">88 accounts have no pattern. Design due 23 October.</p></td><td><p>Marcus Oyelaran</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Tax integration</b></p></td><td><p>Amber</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Live in 34 jurisdictions; 19 EU rounding discrepancies remain.</p></td><td><p>Tomás Iriarte</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Revenue recognition</b></p></td><td><p>Amber</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Design signed off; build start depends on an open decision.</p></td><td><p>Tomás Iriarte</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Self-serve checkout</b></p></td><td><p>Green</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Live since 4 May; redesign waits for Growth's pricing test.</p></td><td><p>Project owner</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Legacy run-off</b></p></td><td><p>Green</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">BillingSvc frozen and read-only for migrated accounts; two engineers on call.</p></td><td><p>Engineering</p></td></tr></tbody></table></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="TAjeS-hsFq"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="mNEfMz-vdv"><p role="eyebrow">STATUS · MIGRATION · S-03</p><h2>Migration is 62% done and the remainder is the hard part</h2><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="l39Onx96Fe" background-color="surface" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><display size="lg">62%</display><h4>707 of 1,140 eligible accounts</h4><p font-size="sm">Moved across eight waves from 4 June to 10 September, averaging 88 accounts per wave.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="JbQgGBQ-zO" vertical-align="center" colspan="40"><graph chart-type="stackedBar" show-data-labels="true" color-scheme="theme" config="{&quot;legend&quot;:{&quot;position&quot;:&quot;top&quot;}}" width="560pt" height="145pt"><properties><property key="base" label="Eligible base" type="label"></property><property key="migrated" label="Migrated" type="data"></property><property key="remaining" label="Remaining" type="data"></property></properties><data><row><cell>Accounts</cell><cell>707</cell><cell>433</cell></row></data></graph><grid spacing="small"><grid-item id="EFeIsGJJGR" colspan="20"><h4>433 remain</h4><p font-size="sm">88 are classed complex.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="FkBpBEZai-" colspan="20"><h4>8 waves left</h4><p font-size="sm">8 October to 14 January, about 54 accounts each.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="wiPULXhunG" colspan="20"><h4>4,190 subscriptions</h4><p font-size="sm">Migrated accounts carry 2,612.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Two completed waves slipped by a week. None was rolled back, and no customer-visible billing outage has been traced to a wave. Wave 15 falls on 31 December.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="YK0hDuElwy"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="gIh8KtwCxm"><p role="eyebrow">STATUS · BUDGET · S-04</p><h2>Budget is forecast 8.75% over, driven by one scope change</h2><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="iIacBxBoZ_" vertical-align="center" colspan="37"><graph chart-type="column" show-data-labels="true" y-axis-min="0" text-size="md" width="520pt" height="285pt"><properties><property key="position" label="Budget position" type="label"></property><property key="amount" label="Amount ($M)" type="data"></property></properties><data><row><cell>Approved</cell><cell>2.4</cell></row><row><cell>Spent to 31 Aug</cell><cell>1.52</cell></row><row><cell>Forecast</cell><cell>2.61</cell></row></data></graph><p role="caption">$2.40M approved: $1.05M vendor, $0.98M internal delivery and $0.37M contingency.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="M5_3ufI_Oh" background-color="surface" vertical-align="center" colspan="23"><display size="md">$210K</display><h4>Forecast overrun</h4><p font-size="sm">The forecast at completion is an assumption: it requires the remaining waves to run at planned effort and Phase 3 to stay within its current design.</p><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="sm"><p font-size="sm"><b>Driver:</b> Tessera Tax, added when Nomad missed 11 jurisdictions. Build cost $164K; the $48K annual licence upsize is unsigned.</p><p font-size="sm"><b>$60K</b> contingency remains. The revised funding paper went to the CFO on 11 September. Chase it in week one.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="gcA8OmoCoP"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="2bMY9psIRz"><p role="eyebrow">STATUS · QUALITY · S-05</p><h2>Invoice accuracy improved fourfold but has stalled short of target</h2><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="efyb3hDur7" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><graph chart-type="column" show-data-labels="true" y-axis-min="0" goal-value="0.5" goal-label="December target" text-size="md" width="505pt" height="285pt"><properties><property key="month" label="Month" type="label"></property><property key="rate" label="Invoices corrected (%)" type="data"></property></properties><data><row><cell>June 2026</cell><cell>4.8</cell></row><row><cell>September 2026</cell><cell>1.3</cell></row></data></graph></grid-item><grid-item id="SdT8Se9zlW" vertical-align="center" colspan="24"><display size="md">31</display><h4>Open exception tickets</h4><table col-widths="[60,20,20]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td><p>Cause</p></td><td><p>Count</p></td><td><p>Share</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>EU tax rounding</p></td><td><p>19</p></td><td><p>61%</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Mid-cycle proration</p></td><td><p>7</p></td><td><p>23%</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Currency timing</p></td><td><p>5</p></td><td><p>16%</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p font-size="sm">The last three weeks show no improvement. The proration adapter needs rework, and that work is not scheduled.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">The same 19 EU rounding tickets appear in the tax workstream and the risk register. One count, three places. The 0.5% target is an assumption chosen in a workshop.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="t3yJ5Se0vk" background-color="heading"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="Z8MwM72HZ-" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><p role="eyebrow">SECTION 03 · HOW IT RUNS</p><h1>How it runs</h1><p font-size="lg">The meetings, systems, incident sequence and commercial terms that keep Meridian operating.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ju4KeT0TD5" padding="0" colspan="24"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/fLDn-Ye8d14676JKlkyth.png" saved-media-id="z6gozj3p1saz29o" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="operational-still-life" alt="Editorial studio photograph of a repeating operational cadence made from warm-white paper cards, operational-blue connector cord looping through evenly spaced graphite clips, one signal-amber gate and one field-sage completed checkpoint, soft directional daylight, precise modular arrangement, no text, lettering, people, logos or screens." meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="rhB7yXEZir"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="81bsmS2bcV"><p role="eyebrow">OPERATIONS · CADENCE · O-01</p><h2>The operating cadence</h2><table col-widths="[23,23,54]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td><p>When</p></td><td><p>Forum</p></td><td><p>What matters</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Monday 09:30</b><br>15 min</p></td><td><p>Squad standup</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Whole delivery team. Blockers only.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Wednesday 14:00</b><br>45 min</p></td><td><p>Wave review</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Hannah chairs; you approve. Go/no-go and exception triage. The review before a wave Thursday is decisive.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Alternate Thursday 16:00</b><br>30 min</p></td><td><p>Steering</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">CFO, CTO and VP RevOps. You present status, budget and decisions sought. Pack due Wednesday noon.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>First 3 business days</b></p></td><td><p>Monthly close check-in</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">With the Controller. Non-negotiable because billing blocks the close.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Quarterly</b></p></td><td><p>Vendor review</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">With Nomad's CSM. Next meeting: 14 October.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><aside><p>Cancel the standup before you cancel the wave review.</p></aside></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="c1CVlSub59"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="xQJWWDRYM8"><p role="eyebrow">OPERATIONS · SYSTEM INDEX · O-02</p><h2>Where everything lives</h2><table col-widths="[25,35,40]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td><p>Need</p></td><td><p>System or location</p></td><td><p>Operational note</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Runbooks and designs</b></p></td><td><p>Confluence · BILL</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Start at “Meridian Home”.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Work tracking</b></p></td><td><p>Jira · MER</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Wave epics are MER-400 to MER-415.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Production access</b></p></td><td><p>IAM · billing-admin</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Request through Access Portal; CTO approval; 24-hour turnaround.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Sandbox</b></p></td><td><p>nomad-sbx-2</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Refreshed from production every Sunday.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Dashboards</b></p></td><td><p>Looker · “Meridian Ops”</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Wave burndown, exception rate and cash collected.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Incidents</b></p></td><td><p>Slack #meridian-oncall</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">PagerDuty service: “Billing Platform”.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Commercial files</b></p></td><td><p>Drive · “Meridian / Commercial”</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Contracts and funding paper; steering-group access only.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="5A5T31i5j3"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="oOwddtqLkA"><p role="eyebrow">OPERATIONS · INCIDENT RUNBOOK · O-03</p><h2>What to do when billing breaks</h2><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" spacing="small" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="OiDArWgJdw" colspan="12"><h4>Declare</h4><p font-size="sm">Post in #meridian-oncall and page Billing Platform. The engineer leads; you handle comms.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="QmSpOhst0J" colspan="12"><h4>Check the wave</h4><p font-size="sm">Incidents have often followed a wave within 72 hours. Rollback: BILL/runbooks/wave-rollback.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ztWbEI5qJh" colspan="12"><h4>Preserve the audit trail</h4><p font-size="sm">Never edit invoices directly. Use a credit note plus reissue or rev-rec breaks.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="07L4ikR-f2" colspan="12"><h4>Open vendor P1</h4><p font-size="sm">Escalate within 30 minutes. The SLA starts at the ticket, not the phone call.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Ee8vIdwO3C" colspan="12"><h4>Tell Finance first</h4><p font-size="sm">The Controller decides whether an invoice run is held. Inform Finance before customers.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="Cx5YMZnEFj"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="L-PQNwJkV7"><p role="eyebrow">OPERATIONS · VENDOR TERMS · O-04</p><h2>The vendor relationship, in the terms that matter</h2><grid divider="sm neutral-border"><grid-item id="fx1BWn8v-u" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><display size="md">$310K</display><h4>Annual contract</h4><p font-size="sm">Three-year term to 31 March 2029.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="X9LDIaIlRk" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><display size="md">90 days</display><h4>Renewal notice</h4><p font-size="sm">Diary 31 December 2028.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="kC-RwsBVjW" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><display size="md">2 hours</display><h4>P1 response</h4><p font-size="sm">P2 response is one business day.</p></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="vMXIj7F_Fu" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><h3>Relationship</h3><p font-size="sm">Nomad Billing. CSM Elena Petrova holds office hours on Thursdays. The relationship is good but transactional; written escalation works, Slack does not.</p><p font-size="sm">SLA credits must be claimed within 30 days. Kestrel has never claimed one.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="k_dWqk-R7u" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><h3>Roadmap commitments</h3><p font-size="sm"><b>Multi-currency payouts:</b> committed for Q1 2027.</p><p font-size="sm"><b>Native EU tax expansion:</b> unscheduled.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="nayuJgI5_R" background-color="heading"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="ri-X1qr-B9" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><p role="eyebrow">SECTION 04 · PEOPLE AND DECISIONS</p><h1>People and decisions</h1><p font-size="lg">Who holds each decision, what is settled and where the unresolved exposure sits.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="oRK_Ow3JLI" padding="0" colspan="24"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/CjYgwqSn2YngrwFwd2OAh.png" saved-media-id="8o2m3pugqold3kk" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="operational-still-life" alt="Editorial studio photograph of modular paper ownership blocks linked by taut operational-blue cord, five field-sage tabs fixed in place and four signal-amber tabs waiting at decision gates, warm-white and graphite materials under soft directional daylight, precise handover system, no text, lettering, people, logos or screens." meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="zBjarMsL5X"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="7iQMH-odn5"><p role="eyebrow">PEOPLE · OWNERSHIP MAP · P-01</p><h2>Who owns what</h2><table col-widths="[27,24,49]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td><p>Person</p></td><td><p>Role</p></td><td><p>Decision boundary</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Dana Whitfield</b></p></td><td><p>CFO · sponsor</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Funding, scope changes and the year-end call. Decides; does not attend detail.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>You</b></p></td><td><p>Project owner</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Delivery, budget, steering pack and every open decision in this pack.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Marcus Oyelaran</b></p></td><td><p>Engineering Lead</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Platform build, proration adapter and complex-account patterns. Sole adapter expert.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Hannah Blum</b></p></td><td><p>RevOps Manager</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Wave planning, customer communications and go/no-go recommendation.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Tomás Iriarte</b></p></td><td><p>Finance Systems Lead</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Tax, revenue recognition and close readiness.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Wei Zhang</b></p></td><td><p>QA</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Wave regression suite and exception triage.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Sanjay Rao</b></p></td><td><p>Data Platform</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Metering API dependency; not a Meridian team member.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p role="caption">Eleven people total. Five engineers report to Marcus, not to you.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="Sn_NUQB9x1"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="aPnr96Z25G"><p role="eyebrow">PEOPLE · DECISION LOG · D-01–D-05</p><h2>Five decisions already made — reopen these only with new evidence</h2><table col-widths="[9,15,29,47]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td><p>ID</p></td><td><p>When</p></td><td><p>Decision</p></td><td><p>Recorded basis</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>D-01</p></td><td><p>Feb 2026</p></td><td><p><b>Buy, not build</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Build was costed at 26 engineer-months against an 18-month deadline.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>D-02</p></td><td><p>Mar 2026</p></td><td><p><b>Waves, not big bang</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Finance would not accept one cutover across a close period.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>D-03</p></td><td><p>Apr 2026</p></td><td><p><b>Tessera over Nomad tax</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Nomad covered 23 of 34 jurisdictions. This caused the overrun; my judgment is that it was still the right call.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>D-04</p></td><td><p>May 2026</p></td><td><p><b>Keep BillingSvc read-only</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Audit needs FY26 and FY27 history queryable.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>D-05</p></td><td><p>Jul 2026</p></td><td><p><b>Exclude 40 perpetual accounts</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">They run off by FY28; migration cost exceeded remaining revenue. This sets the denominator at 1,140.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="Ef4GoS-fUp"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="jQdrOkVXdQ"><p role="eyebrow">PEOPLE · OPEN DECISIONS · A-01–A-04</p><h2>Four decisions are waiting for you</h2><grid spacing="small" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="p7beYMtIX9" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><labels><label variant="solid">A-01 · Due 6 Nov</label></labels><h4>Revenue recognition before or after year-end close?</h4><p font-size="sm">A pre-close launch puts rev-rec and the close on Tomás in the same three weeks. Waiting creates two months of manual schedules. Sponsor: CFO.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="aid5N-u1mJ" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><labels><label variant="solid">A-02 · Due 16 Oct</label></labels><h4>Who owns dunning policy?</h4><p font-size="sm">Finance and Customer Success each say the other team owns it. The answer blocks Phase 3 build.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="gNEutgA7OI" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><labels><label variant="solid">A-03 · Due 30 Oct</label></labels><h4>Sign the $48K Tessera upsize?</h4><p font-size="sm">The current tier caps at 25,000 calculations a month. August reached 23,100.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="hHppaLbbQw" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><labels><label variant="solid">A-04 · Steering</label></labels><h4>Set a BillingSvc decommission date</h4><p font-size="sm">It is unfunded, unowned and costs $7K a month in hosting. A steering date makes it real.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="U6yKGYta1q"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="EXHmb1qZKo"><p role="eyebrow">PEOPLE · RISK REGISTER · R-01–R-07</p><h2>Risk register</h2><table col-widths="[8,28,16,48]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false" style="--table-cell-padding-block: 4pt; --table-cell-padding-inline: 12pt;"><tbody><tr><td><p>ID</p></td><td><p>Risk</p></td><td><p>Rating</p></td><td><p>Mitigation and owner</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>R-01</p></td><td><p><b>Complex-account migration slips</b></p></td><td><p>High · likely</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">88 accounts; no pattern; design due 23 October. Marcus is prototyping three archetypes. Fallback: extend waves into February. Owner: Marcus.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>R-02</p></td><td><p><b>Proration key-person dependency</b></p></td><td><p>High</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Marcus alone understands the adapter. Pairing was cancelled twice. Unresolved. Owner: you.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>R-03</p></td><td><p><b>Wave 15 on 31 December</b></p></td><td><p>Medium</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Holiday cover is thin and Finance is closed. Moving it shifts the last wave to 28 January. Decide 16 December. Owner: Hannah.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>R-04</p></td><td><p><b>EU tax rounding</b></p></td><td><p>Medium</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">The same 19 customer-visible tickets. Owner: Tomás.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>R-05</p></td><td><p><b>Budget approval refused or trimmed</b></p></td><td><p>Medium</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Would stop the Tessera upsize and cap throughput. Owner: you.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>R-06</p></td><td><p><b>January close contention</b></p></td><td><p>Medium</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Finance capacity is fully committed in weeks 1–3. Owner: Tomás.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>R-07</p></td><td><p><b>Vendor slips multi-currency payouts</b></p></td><td><p>Low · contractual</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Q1 2027 commitment; APAC expansion depends on it. Owner: you.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="6Iu3d0-W04"><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="MleFrPgc1t" vertical-align="center" colspan="23"><p role="eyebrow">PEOPLE · DEPENDENCIES · X-01</p><h2>Four things you depend on and do not control</h2><p font-size="sm"><b>Metering API v3:</b> Data Platform, due 20 November. Sanjay Rao flags a two-week risk. Check weekly.</p><p font-size="sm"><b>CPQ mapping freeze:</b> Kira Lund agreed no schema changes until 31 January. Get it in email.</p><p font-size="sm"><b>Tessera approval:</b> Procurement needs two weeks after the CFO decision.</p><p font-size="sm"><b>Growth experiment:</b> runs to 30 November. Checkout redesign waits.</p><p role="caption">The PCI scope-change security review closed on 12 August.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="k2fhBpP556" align="center" vertical-align="center" colspan="37"><diagram template-key="inputs" width="520pt" height="340pt" data-meta="{&quot;general&quot;:[{&quot;text&quot;:&quot;<h4>Meridian delivery</h4>&quot;}],&quot;step&quot;:[{&quot;text&quot;:&quot;<h4>Metering API v3</h4><p>Data Platform · 20 Nov</p>&quot;},{&quot;text&quot;:&quot;<h4>CPQ mapping freeze</h4><p>Deal Desk · through 31 Jan</p>&quot;},{&quot;text&quot;:&quot;<h4>Tessera approval</h4><p>Procurement · two-week cycle</p>&quot;},{&quot;text&quot;:&quot;<h4>Growth experiment</h4><p>Runs through 30 Nov</p>&quot;}]}"></diagram></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="VfDeWpyeDb"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="UOwmAvhcta"><p role="eyebrow">PEOPLE · UNANSWERED QUESTIONS · Q-01</p><h2>Open questions nobody has answered</h2><table col-widths="[42,58]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td><p>Question</p></td><td><p>Why it cannot wait</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Who owns billing after Meridian closes?</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">There is no permanent operating team. Decide before Phase 3, not after.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>What is the real invoice-accuracy target?</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">The 0.5% figure came from a workshop and was never validated against customer tolerance. Treat it as an assumption.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Will the 41 bespoke arrangements be standardised?</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Sales has resisted twice. Migrating them as-is embeds them for years.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Is the three-year payback still credible?</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">The original assumption included no tax engine and a FY27 decommission. Neither holds.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Should 40 perpetual accounts run off untouched?</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Nobody has rechecked July's carve-out against $7K a month of BillingSvc hosting.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="Z1obVLuKMS"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="yM8p7YE1nq"><p role="eyebrow">FIRST 90 DAYS · ACTION PLAN · A-05</p><h2>Your first ninety days</h2><p>Day one is 1 October. The blocks end on 30 October, 29 November and 29 December.</p><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" spacing="medium" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="ZLJkvZWRjY" colspan="20"><h3>Days 1–30</h3><p font-size="sm">Chase funding. Observe the 8 and 22 October waves without changing them. Join the 14 October vendor review while I chair it. Read the proration design with Marcus and restore the pairing sessions. Resolve dunning ownership by 16 October. Sign or refuse the Tessera upsize by 30 October.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="4WdOiASnn7" colspan="20"><h3>Days 31–60</h3><p font-size="sm">Take the complex-account design to steering with a dated plan. Land the rev-rec timing decision by 6 November. Get the CPQ freeze in writing. Check Metering API v3 with Sanjay before 20 November. Name the permanent owner of billing operations.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="CP_2c8sHLS" colspan="20"><h3>Days 61–90</h3><p font-size="sm">Settle the 31 December wave at the 16 December review. Reforecast Meridian with Phase 3 properly scoped. Set the BillingSvc decommission date. Validate or replace the accuracy target. Book the January vendor review and chair it yourself.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="-hb-ewtR0e"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="mrIJr4JsL5"><p role="eyebrow">FIRST 90 DAYS · WEEK ONE · A-06</p><h2>Week one, and how to reach me</h2><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="T7Aw2grRKX" colspan="38"><grid divider="sm neutral-border" marker="number" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-inline-size: 30pt; --marker-gap: 12pt;"><grid-item id="W4WTnzhFVh" padding="8pt 0"><h4>Request billing-admin on day one</h4><p font-size="sm">It takes 24 hours and blocks everything else.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="YUaCAHPLkM" padding="8pt 0"><h4>Read BILL/Meridian Home end to end</h4><p font-size="sm">Allow two hours. It is current to 19 September.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="6rHlAF8t-a" padding="8pt 0"><h4>Meet Marcus, Hannah and Tomás</h4><p font-size="sm">See each of them individually before your first steering.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="U_KphBT1wz" padding="8pt 0"><h4>Observe the 7 October wave review</h4><p font-size="sm">It is the day before wave 9 ships. Say nothing.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Etjado90dp" padding="8pt 0"><h4>Chase the funding paper</h4><p font-size="sm">Go through the CFO's EA, not the CFO.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="spQrWAAr9I" background-color="accent" vertical-align="center" colspan="22"><p role="eyebrow">HANDOVER TERMS</p><h3>I shadow you until 9 October.</h3><p>I answer questions until 30 October.</p><hr thickness="md" width="sm"><p font-size="sm">After that I am on Data Platform. The escalation path is Marcus, then the CTO.</p><spacer size="18pt"></spacer><p font-size="sm">Priya Raghunathan · outgoing owner<br>Pack written 23 September 2026</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>